Source: snooze
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Robert Tulke <rt@ttyS0.sh>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/rtulke/snooze
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: snooze
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.8)
Recommends: bash-completion
Description: temporarily mute Zabbix hosts and hostgroups
 snooze creates and removes time-boxed Zabbix Maintenance windows via the
 Zabbix JSON-RPC API (Bearer token auth, requires Zabbix >= 6.4), so hosts
 or entire hostgroups can be muted for a fixed duration - or for a window
 scheduled to start later via "snooze plan" - without leaving noise behind:
 muting an already-muted target updates its existing window in place
 instead of deleting and recreating it.
 .
 All output is available in German and English, chosen automatically from
 the system locale (or pinned via the 'lang' config key).
 .
 See snooze(1) and /etc/snooze.conf.example after installing.
